  "title": "Simit",
  "subtitle": "Turkish sesame bread rings with a crisp, seed-encrusted crust",
  "excerpt": "Simit are circular Turkish bread rings sold by street vendors throughout Turkey, particularly in Istanbul where they arrive hot each morning on trays balanced on vendors' heads. The distinctive feature is a thick, even coat of sesame seeds bonded to the dough by dipping the rings in diluted grape molasses before rolling in seeds. The crust bakes crisp and nutty; the inside is soft with a slight chew. They are at their best eaten the day they are made.",
  "type": "RECIPE",
